James sought advice on displaying labeled percentages on a map in R, noting the challenge of representing both reasonable (16%) and very small values (3e-4%). He was using a function to format these percentages but had concerns about the presentation of scientific notation, particularly the unwanted "e" notation and the zero in the exponent. I suggested focusing on clarity by removing unnecessary elements and using typographic improvements. I recommended an R function that formats small percentages in a more visually appealing way while considering the audience. The function outputs standard percentages for readable values and employs a simplified notation for smaller percentages, ensuring clarity and elegance in presentation.
